#: src/seq.c:80
#, c-format
msgid ""
"Usage: %s [OPTION]... LAST\n"
"  or:  %s [OPTION]... FIRST LAST\n"
"  or:  %s [OPTION]... FIRST INCREMENT LAST\n"
msgstr ""
"Upotreba: %s [OPCIJA]... POSLEDNJA\n"
"  ili:  %s [OPCIJA]... PRVA POSLEDNJA\n"
"  ili:  %s [OPCIJA]... PRVA INKREMENT POSLEDNJA\n"

#: src/seq.c:85
msgid "Print numbers from FIRST to LAST, in steps of INCREMENT.\n"
msgstr "Ispisati brojeve od FIRST do LAST, u koracima INCREMENT-a.\n"

#: src/seq.c:91
msgid ""
"  -f, --format=FORMAT      use printf style floating-point FORMAT\n"
"  -s, --separator=STRING   use STRING to separate numbers (default: \\n)\n"
"  -w, --equal-width        equalize width by padding with leading zeroes\n"
msgstr ""
"  -f, --format=FORMAT      koristiti prinf stil floating-point FORMAT\n"
"  -s, --separator=STRING   koristiti STRING za razdvajanje brojeva (default: "
"\\n)\n"
"  -w, --equal-width        izjednači širinu ubacivanjem vodećih nula\n"

#: src/seq.c:98
msgid ""
"\n"
"If FIRST or INCREMENT is omitted, it defaults to 1.  That is, an\n"
"omitted INCREMENT defaults to 1 even when LAST is smaller than FIRST.\n"
"The sequence of numbers ends when the sum of the current number and\n"
"INCREMENT would become greater than LAST.\n"
"FIRST, INCREMENT, and LAST are interpreted as floating point values.\n"
"INCREMENT is usually positive if FIRST is smaller than LAST, and\n"
"INCREMENT is usually negative if FIRST is greater than LAST.\n"
"INCREMENT must not be 0; none of FIRST, INCREMENT and LAST may be NaN.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"ako FIRST ili INCREMENT je izostavljen, ide na zadno po 1.  TO jest,\n"
"izostavljeni INCREMENT ide po zadanom na 1 čak i kad je LAST manji od "
"FIRST.\n"
"Sekvenca brojeva završava kad bi sume trenutnih brojeva i\n"
"INCREMENT postale vee od LAST.\n"
"FIRST, INCREMENT, i LAST se gledaju kao realne vrijednosti.\n"
"INCREMENT je obično pozitivan ako je FIRST manji od LAST, i\n"
"INCREMENT je obično negativan ako je FIRST veči od LAST.\n"
"INCREMENT ne smije biti nula 0; niti jedan od FIRST, INCREMENT i LAST ne "
"smiju biti NaN.\n"

#: src/seq.c:109
msgid ""
"FORMAT must be suitable for printing one argument of type 'double';\n"
"it defaults to %.PRECf if FIRST, INCREMENT, and LAST are all fixed point\n"
"decimal numbers with maximum precision PREC, and to %g otherwise.\n"
msgstr ""
"FORMAT mora biti prikladan za štampanje jednog argumenta tipa „double“;\n"
"podrazumijevano je %.PRECf ako su PRVI, INKREMENT i POSLJEDNJI decimalni "
"brojevi\n"
"sa fiksiranim zarezom sa najvećom preciznošću PREC, i na %g inače.\n"

